Let WinSCP's .NET assembly drive the executable over inherited pipes off Windows.

Off Windows .NET has no named events or file mappings, so the assembly
cannot hand the executable winscp.com's TConsoleCommStruct. It now starts
the executable with /console /consolepipes=<read>,<write> -- two inherited
anonymous pipes -- and passes the whole structure back and forth over them:
the protocol is otherwise unchanged. Windows, and net40, keep the events and
the file mapping. See doc/qt/adr/0010-console-pipes.md.

Offered upstream as winscp/winscp#73. Applied by port/tools/build_winscpnet.py
to a copy of dotnet/, not by patchset.py: the assembly is not part of the
line-preserving generated tree, and this patch adds lines.

